`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["For initial mTLS, ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"client_certificate_settings"})," contains ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"validation_cas"}),", ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"allow_expired"}),", ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"chain_level_validation"})," and ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"allow_unverifiable_revocation"}),". The validator receives one certificate credential; the flow does not guarantee forwarding every handshake intermediate to it. For a direct case, configure the bootstrap’s direct issuer as validation CA and test the actual Gateway path."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["The authentication editor offers an ",e.jsx(i.strong,{children:"Allow certificates without revocation information"})," switch (",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"allow_unverifiable_revocation"}),", off by default). When it is on, certificates (and intermediate CAs of the chain) that Lamassu does not manage and that list no OCSP or CRL endpoint are accepted; unreachable, stale or inconclusive revocation answers are always rejected. While the switch is on, the console shows an amber warning: ",e.jsx(i.strong,{children:"Revocation will not be verified"}),". A revoked certificate with no OCSP or CRL endpoint, and not managed by Lamassu, will be accepted, and this also applies to the intermediate CAs of the chain."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["The same switch is offered in both the enrollment and re-enrollment authentication editors and is stored per block inside ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"est_rfc7030_settings.client_certificate_settings"}),"; a DMS stored before this field existed loads with the switch off. The console also shows an amber warning alert whenever an authentication option is in its insecure state (",e.jsx(i.strong,{children:"Allow expired certificates"})," on, ",e.jsx(i.strong,{children:"Allow expired renewal"})," on or ",e.jsx(i.strong,{children:"Verify CSR signature"})," off) and the No authentication note is presented as a warning alert too."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["Revocation is checked for every presented certificate. In initial enrollment the client certificate ",e.jsx(i.strong,{children:"and"})," every intermediate CA between it and the validation CA are checked, each against its issuer; extra certificates the device sends in the handshake are ignored. A validation CA that is revoked in Lamassu rejects the operation: the first validation CA that validates the certificate is used, and a revoked one is not replaced by the remaining validation CAs. Certificates issued and managed by Lamassu are checked against their stored status. External certificates are checked through their OCSP and CRL endpoints, and the operation fails closed when revocation cannot be verified: only ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"allow_unverifiable_revocation"})," (",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"false"})," by default in both blocks) relaxes the case of an external certificate that lists no endpoint at all. Endpoints that exist but are unreachable, return stale or invalid evidence, or report an inconclusive status are always rejected, whatever the option says. The details and the evidence the endpoints must present are in ",e.jsx(i.a,{href:"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/est/bootstrap-identity#revocation-and-checks",children:"Revocation and checks"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["For certificate re-enrollment, the validator tries the enrollment CA first and then the CAs listed in ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"reenrollment_settings.est_rfc7030_settings.client_certificate_settings.validation_cas"}),"; those are the re-enrollment validation CAs. That list is optional because the enrollment CA is always trusted for re-enrollment, and each settings block consults only its own ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"validation_cas"}),". CAs listed only in the initial block's ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"validation_cas"})," do not extend re-enrollment acceptance; during a CA rotation, add the old issuance CA to the re-enrollment block's list. The re-enrollment validator compares the presented TLS leaf against those CAs; the re-enrollment block's ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"chain_level_validation"})," and ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"allow_expired"})," values are stored but not consulted, and expiry is governed by ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"enable_expired_renewal"}),". Re-enrollment checks revocation of the client certificate only; that check is governed by the re-enrollment block's own ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"allow_unverifiable_revocation"}),"."]}),`
